<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Prinzenstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1784</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Prinzenstein is a fort built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> in 1784 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keta">Keta</a>, on the coast of south-eastern Ghana. It protected Danish trade, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>, on the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> and served as a holding place for enslaved people. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> bought it with the other Danish forts in 1850; much of it has since been destroyed by coastal erosion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-prinzenstein.jpg" alt="Fort Prinzenstein" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: coollessons · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FortPrinzestein2KetaGhana1970AD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
